      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨xy,zy,zx⟩$ and $f(x,y,z)=xyz,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨yz,xz,xy⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(zy)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(zx)=y+z+x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =xyz(x+y+z)+⟨xy,zy,zx⟩\\cdot ⟨yz,xz,xy⟩ \\\\  & =xyz(x+y+z)+x{y}^{2}z+xy{z}^{2}+{x}^{2}yz \\\\  & =xyz(x+y+z)+xyz(x+y+z) \\\\  & =2xyz(x+y+z).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Correct",
